$1.7&nbsp;million and $1.5&nbsp;million, for the three months ended July&nbsp;31, 2026 and 2025, respectively. The difference between GAAP and <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">non-GAAP</FONT> gross margin was 1.6% and 1.8%, or $3.2&nbsp;million and
$3.2&nbsp;million, for the six months ended July&nbsp;31, 2026 and 2025, respectively. The differences were due to the effect of stock-based compensation and acquisition-related costs. </P>
